<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melkote</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Melukote</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Melkote is a hill town in Mandya district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, and a major centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-vaishnavism">Sri Vaishnavism</a>. The philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramanuja">Ramanuja</a> lived there for about twelve years in the early 12th century, and its Cheluvanarayana Swamy temple and hilltop Yoga Narasimha temple remain important places of pilgrimage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/melkote.jpg" alt="Melkote" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philanthropist 1 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melukotetemple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
